      "writtenOn": "2024-05-08T16:44:47Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "\u003e Where is the panic coming from ?\n\n`shared` is the result (as in `core::result::Result`) of the HVC and `.unwrap()` will make Rust panic if it is not `Ok` (i.e. if the HVC hasn\u0027t return `0` in x0) because that then means that we have - somehow - failed to actually \"unshare\" the page. As `handle_mmio_fault` is running in fault-handling context and corresponding the PTE has already been updated at this point (i.e. stage-1 will allow valid accesses), what should we otherwise do?\n\nIf we undo the stage-1 mapping (which is annoying to get right, given BBM), the access we\u0027ve trapped will be replayed and will result in a stage-1 page fault (and possibly infinite loop, except if we unset the SW bit). OTOH, if we leave the page table as-is, the replayed access will result in a stage-2 fault and pvmfw mysteriously dying.\n\nInstead, panicking at this point seems to make the most sense?\n\nDo you want me to add more details to the comment above?\n\n\u003e Are we doing PSCI_MEM_PROTECT before ending up here ?\n\nIsn\u0027t `PSCI_MEM_PROTECT` only issued by the hypervisor; I\u0027m not how that affects this code?",
